    {
      "title": "Module 2: Frequency Adverbs",
      "subtopics": [],
      "lessons": [
        {
          "title": "Always, Often, Sometimes, Never",
          "weight": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "order": 1,
              "type": "text",
              "content": "{\"time\":1700000303000,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"qR9sT0uV1w\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Frequency adverbs</b> tell us how often we do something. In order from most to least frequent:\"}},{\"id\":\"xY2zA3bC4d\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"ordered\",\"items\":[\"<b>always</b> (100%) — <em>I always read before bed.</em>\",\"<b>usually</b> (80–90%) — <em>She usually cooks dinner.</em>\",\"<b>often</b> (70%) — <em>We often go cycling.</em>\",\"<b>sometimes</b> (30–50%) — <em>He sometimes watches films.</em>\",\"<b>rarely / seldom</b> (10%) — <em>I rarely go dancing.</em>\",\"<b>never</b> (0%) — <em>She never plays video games.</em>\"]}},{\"id\":\"eF5gH6iJ7k\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Position:</b> Frequency adverbs go <b>before the main verb</b> but <b>after 'to be'</b>:<br><em>I <u>always</u> drink coffee. / She is <u>never</u> late.</em>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.4\"}"
            },
            {
              "order": 2,
              "type": "audio",
              "content": {
                "text": "I always read before bed. She is never late. We sometimes go cycling.",
                "type": "tts",
                "audio_url": ""
              }
            },
