              "title": "Going to the Cinema and Theatre",
              "weight": 4,
              "content": [
                {
                  "order": 1,
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "{\"time\":1700000304000,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"lM8nO9pQ0r\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Going out is a popular leisure activity. Useful vocabulary for entertainment:\"}},{\"id\":\"sT1uV2wX3y\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"<b>cinema / movie theatre</b> — a place to watch films\",\"<b>theatre</b> — a place to watch live performances\",\"<b>concert</b> — a live music performance\",\"<b>gallery</b> — a place to see art\",\"<b>exhibition</b> — a collection of items on display\",\"<b>show</b> — a performance of any kind\"]}},{\"id\":\"zA4bC5dE6f\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Phrases for inviting someone:</b><br><em>Would you like to go to the cinema? / Do you fancy seeing a film? / How about going to a concert?</em>\"}},{\"id\":\"gH7iJ8kL9m\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Accepting / declining:</b><br><em>Yes, I'd love to! / That sounds great! / I'm afraid I can't. / Maybe another time.</em>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.4\"}"
                },
